    "chapter_number": 3,
    "chapter_name": "constitutional design",
    "question_type": "multipart",
    "question_text": "Here are different opinions about what made India a democracy. How much importance would you give to each of these factors?",
    "question_latex": null,
    "mcq_options": [],
    "correct_option": null,
    "question_image": {
      "present": false,
      "description": null,
      "cloudinary_url": null,
      "latex_extracted": null,
      "source_page_number": null,
      "source_image_index": null,
      "ownership": "unknown"
    },
    "parts": [
      {
        "part_label": "(a)",
        "part_text": "Democracy in India is a gift of the British rulers. We received training to work with representative legislative institutions under the British rule.",
        "part_latex": null,
        "answer_text": "The importance of this fact cannot be ignored. We should acknowledge that we learnt many good things from the British rulers and democracy was one of them.",
        "answer_latex": null,
        "steps": [],
        "final_answer": "Thus, the British influence played a significant role in shaping Indian democracy.",
        "answer_image": {
          "present": false,
          "description": null,
          "cloudinary_url": null,
          "latex_extracted": null,
          "source_page_number": null,
          "source_image_index": null,
          "ownership": "unknown"
        },
        "question_images": [],
        "answer_images": [],
        "question_image": {
          "present": false,
          "description": null,
          "cloudinary_url": null,
          "latex_extracted": null,
          "source_page_number": null,
          "source_image_index": null,
          "ownership": "unknown"
        }
      },
      {
        "part_label": "(b)",
        "part_text": "Freedom Struggle challenged the colonial exploitation and denial of different freedoms to Indians. Free India could not be anything but democratic.",
        "part_latex": null,
        "answer_text": "Freedom struggle was important in spreading the idea of nationalism in India and inculcating the practice of making decisions by consensus.",
        "answer_latex": null,
        "steps": [],
        "final_answer": "Therefore, the freedom struggle was crucial in establishing democratic values.",
        "answer_image": {
          "present": false,
          "description": null,
          "cloudinary_url": null,
          "latex_extracted": null,
          "source_page_number": null,
          "source_image_index": null,
          "ownership": "unknown"
        },
        "question_images": [],
        "answer_images": [],
        "question_image": {
          "present": false,
          "description": null,
          "cloudinary_url": null,
          "latex_extracted": null,
          "source_page_number": null,
          "source_image_index": null,
          "ownership": "unknown"
        }
      },
      {
        "part_label": "(c)",
        "part_text": "We were lucky to have leaders who had democratic convictions. The denial of democracy in several other newly independent countries shows the important role of these leaders.",
        "part_latex": null,
        "answer_text": "We were indeed lucky that we did not have leaders who were autocratic. India’s freedom struggle is the only example of a bloodless freedom struggle in the contemporary history. This could be possible because our nationalist leaders had the maturity to listen to others’ views.",
        "answer_latex": null,
        "steps": [],
        "final_answer": "Thus, the democratic convictions of our leaders were vital for India's democratic journey.",
        "answer_image": {
          "present": false,
          "description": null,
          "cloudinary_url": null,
          "latex_extracted": null,
          "source_page_number": null,
          "source_image_index": null,
          "ownership": "unknown"
        },
